===Locating your logfile (Windows)===

For [[EverQuest Titanium]] client, the player event & chat logs are helpful for various research and investigation. Here is some helpful info on the subject of logging.

Typically, it is located in
   C:\Program Files (x86)\Sony\EverQuest\Logs\

====Windows 10====
:'''''See also: [[Windows 10]]'''''

On more recent versions of Windows 10 (2017 and beyond), files are located in User Profile info:

 C:\Users\<your username>\AppData\Local\VirtualStore\Program Files (x86)\Sony\EverQuest\Logs\

   C:\ (logical drive)
    '''Users'''
     '''<your username>'''
      '''AppData''' (hidden folder)
       '''Local'''
        '''VirtualStore'''
         Program Files (x86)
          Sony
           EverQuest
            Logs

====Other issues====

Administrative privileges and [https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/help/975787/guided-help-adjust-user-account-control-settings-in-windows-7-and-wind User Account Control] often mess with eqgame.exe. There are lots of helpful posts in the [https://www.project1999.com/forums/forumdisplay.php?f=40 Technical Discussion] forum.

===Enabling Logging===

You can type <code>/log on</code> to enable logging for a session, or edit the <code>eqclient.ini</code> file to reflect <code>Log=TRUE</code> if you wish to enable it permanently. The <code>eqclient.ini</code> file will be located in the EverQuest folder noted in the section above according to your OS.

